# Build context for docker/Dockerfile.
#
# The image only ever needs pyproject.toml, README.md, LICENSE, src/ and the
# three preset configs, so this is written as "deny everything, then re-allow"
# rather than as a blocklist.  A blocklist silently starts shipping whatever a
# future commit adds -- and the things most likely to be added here are the
# multi-gigabyte assembly downloads under data/ and the run outputs under
# results/.

*

!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src

# `kmer-dust init-config --preset <name>` reads these at run time; the
# Dockerfile copies them to /opt/kmer-dust/presets.  Re-allowing the directory
# is not enough on its own -- docker needs the parent un-ignored too, which is
# why both lines are here.
!workflow
!workflow/config
!workflow/config/*.yaml

# ...and nothing compiled, cached or downloaded from inside src/.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.so
**/*.egg-info
**/.DS_Store
